Execution prompt revision
=========================

source: k8s-agentic-operator (private)
commit: cb1ed3b6462feaa090c4c7b3c273753c7aece20b
date: 2026-09-11

execution.txt is copied byte-for-byte from the committed
agent/prompts/minimal/execution.txt at this revision, not its working tree.
The shipped roles/execution.txt changes only {{KUBECTL_MODE_PROMPT}} to
{{KUBECTL_GUIDANCE}}, the marker rename used by the original migration.

execution.composed.txt is rendered from that source prompt with the same revision's
agent/prompts/shared/kubectl/safe.execution.txt: strip both texts, replace
{{KUBECTL_MODE_PROMPT}} with the block, and add no newline. No MAVER loader is used
to generate this expected output. Execution declares no memory marker, so this
output applies with memory both enabled and disabled.

This revision confines Execution to confirming that the planned mutations landed.
Application recovery is judged separately; a successfully applied plan cannot be
handed back merely because the incident persists. The prompt is therefore a changed
experimental input, not a correction to the record of earlier measurements.

The preceding prompt remains byte-for-byte in
tests/fixtures/prototype/agent/prompts/minimal/execution.txt and its composed outputs
remain in tests/fixtures/composed_prompts/execution.memory_{on,off}.txt. Historical
composition tests replay that prompt through override_dir; new-default tests use
the versioned files here. Do not replace those historical fixtures in a refreeze.
